1
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:06,480
Do you like it?

2
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,340
In Nanhuai's climate,

3
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:11,420
lilacs are really hard to grow.

4
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:14,620
This one somehow has buds.

5
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:18,320
As long as you like it,

6
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:19,750
no matter how hard it is,

7
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,200
I'll do it.

8
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:25,460
That's very thoughtful of you.

9
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:27,620
But you're busy with military affairs.

10
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:29,270
No need to waste your time.

11
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:32,400
Once flowers bloom,

12
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,340
they always wither.

13
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:37,080
What's the point of obsessing

14
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:38,700
over whether they bloom?

15
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:01,930
Sitting here all alone,

16
00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:03,030
you must be so bored.

17
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:04,780
Would you like to join Mrs. Gu

18
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:06,100
for a few rounds of mahjong?

19
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:08,900
Mother, you're doing a favor
for Changxuan.

20
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,760
It's safest if you handle it personally.

21
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,700
My dear child,

22
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:14,500
you see everything so clearly,

23
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:16,780
except when it comes to yourself.

24
00:03:21,670 --> 00:03:23,220
How are things with Bingwen lately?

25
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:26,180
Pretty good.

26
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:29,320
Always this answer:

27
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:30,130
"Pretty good."

28
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:41,200
You still haven't gotten over him.

29
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,960
I know it still weighs on you.

30
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,940
You blame your father
for breaking you two up.

31
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:54,760
I let go of the past a long time ago.

32
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:58,990
Besides, the dead don't come back.

33
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:01,280
He's already gone.

34
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:02,950
Dwelling on it

35
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:05,420
is useless.

36
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:10,060
In a family like ours,

37
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:13,270
marriage was never ours to choose.

38
00:04:13,930 --> 00:04:15,860
There's no time to think

39
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:17,290
about love or romance.

40
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,940
When your father and I married,

41
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:23,180
it was just a match between equals.

42
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:25,660
But over the years,

43
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:27,840
through thick and thin,

44
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:29,750
we had you kids

45
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:31,630
and built this home together.

46
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:33,080
Eventually,

47
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:36,320
we became inseparable.

48
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:41,550
Trust me.

49
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,200
I can tell

50
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,840
that Bingwen truly loves you.

51
00:04:55,370 --> 00:04:56,790
You can't stay trapped

52
00:04:56,790 --> 00:04:59,180
in your past forever.

53
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:01,800
Life is about moving forward.

54
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:03,170
Okay, sweetheart?

55
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:04,060
Let's go play.

56
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:04,840
Mother...

57
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:05,940
Come on.

58
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:19,060
It smells so good.

59
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:20,640
All your favorites.

60
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:24,180
And your favorite osmanthus cake.

61
00:05:24,540 --> 00:05:25,140
Try it.

62
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:25,680
Okay.

63
00:05:31,750 --> 00:05:32,220
How is it?

64
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:34,930
It tastes just right.

65
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,030
All these years abroad,

66
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:39,270
I missed your cooking most, Mrs. Ye.

67
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,740
Slow down while you eat.

68
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:43,220
Stop sweet-talking

69
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:44,160
my mother.

70
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:46,820
Xueting,

71
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,380
while you were on your own

72
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:49,400
studying abroad,

73
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:51,170
you still sent me medicine.

74
00:05:51,450 --> 00:05:52,870
You must've cut back on yourself.

75
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:54,230
I feel terrible

76
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,840
about it.

77
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:59,390
You and my mother were sworn sisters.

78
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:01,710
After my mother passed away,

79
00:06:02,420 --> 00:06:03,230
I was only six or seven

80
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,600
when I grew up at your side.

81
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,060
In my heart,

82
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:07,840
honoring you

83
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,570
is the same as honoring my mother.

84
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:14,670
Have some fish.

85
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:18,070
By the way, Xueting,

86
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:20,050
you came back early this time.

87
00:06:20,260 --> 00:06:22,560
Why didn't you mention it
in your letter?

88
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:28,700
I wanted to give you and Pingjun

89
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:29,900
a surprise.

90
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:32,180
Besides, the world is in turmoil.

91
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:33,660
I wanted to come back early

92
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:34,380
to look for opportunities

93
00:06:34,840 --> 00:06:35,630
and secure a job.

94
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:38,820
When Xueting was just twelve,

95
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:40,670
he already wrote brilliantly.

96
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:41,340
Otherwise,

97
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:42,690
how did he get
government-funded study abroad?

98
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:43,950
You

99
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:45,520
will definitely find a job

100
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:47,100
where you can put your talents to use.

101
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:47,700
Definitely.

102
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:53,970
So, this time,

103
00:06:53,970 --> 00:06:55,040
where are you planning to stay?

104
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:57,360
I rented a small courtyard.

105
00:06:57,780 --> 00:06:58,620
It's just one hutong away.

106
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:00,100
That way,

107
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,480
I can take good care of you both.

108
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:44,580
Pingjun.

109
00:08:45,660 --> 00:08:46,340
Do you remember?

110
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:48,200
When we were kids, we did this too.

111
00:08:48,980 --> 00:08:49,770
Whenever the weather was nice,

112
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:51,300
I'd grab a bamboo pole,

113
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:53,150
take you to catch

114
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:54,420
cicadas and crickets,

115
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:57,520
and mix mud to block ant holes.

116
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:59,260
Of course I remember.

117
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:00,630
When we were kids,

118
00:09:00,630 --> 00:09:02,300
we went to the same private school.

119
00:09:02,620 --> 00:09:04,080
When we skipped school to play,

120
00:09:04,470 --> 00:09:05,130
you'd take me

121
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:06,620
to climb the wall behind the school.

122
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:09,600
Beside that wall,

123
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:11,020
there was a pomegranate tree.

124
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:13,340
You were always pestering me

125
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:14,670
to pick pomegranates for you.

126
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:16,370
Once,

127
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,570
I accidentally fell off the wall

128
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,470
and got a huge bump on my head.

129
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:21,770
It just wouldn't go away.

130
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:23,490
What about now?

131
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:25,380
Has it gone down?

132
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:29,730
Here, feel it

133
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:30,860
and see if it's gone.

134
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:43,550
Pingjun,

135
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,880
these four years in Japan,

136
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:47,450
I often felt

137
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:49,600
the surroundings were unfamiliar,

138
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:51,750
and the language kept me at a distance.

139
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:54,080
Even the food

140
00:09:55,680 --> 00:09:56,800
tasted of loneliness.

141
00:09:58,820 --> 00:09:59,980
At times like that,

142
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:02,480
I would think of you.

143
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:07,430
Sometimes,

144
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:10,540
I even missed you like crazy.

145
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,920
Why are you suddenly saying this?

146
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:18,760
It's not sudden.

147
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:21,920
I've kept this in my heart
for a long time.

148
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:27,970
We...

149
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:29,480
Weren't we betrothed

150
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,390
as children?

151
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:32,670
We were too young back then.

152
00:10:33,660 --> 00:10:34,300
So,

153
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:35,550
I want to ask you again, properly.

154
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:38,450
After graduation,

155
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:42,870
will you marry me?

156
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:01,840
No.

157
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:05,430
You lied to me.

158
00:11:05,770 --> 00:11:06,690
You said you wouldn't be back

159
00:11:06,690 --> 00:11:07,420
for a month.

160
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:11,080
I promise

161
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:11,920
that from now on,

162
00:11:12,620 --> 00:11:13,940
I'll never hide anything from you again.

163
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:16,440
Let me see how you behave.

164
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:20,760
Come on!

165
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:23,780
Wait for me!

166
00:11:24,060 --> 00:11:25,480
Come on!

167
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:34,180
Let's go.

168
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:11,140
Are you okay?

169
00:12:13,620 --> 00:12:14,180
I'm fine.

170
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:29,300
What's got you so fascinated?

171
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:31,480
The Chunfeng Troupe

172
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:33,140
has done a great job.

173
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:34,940
All on their own,

174
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:37,170
they changed the refugees' fate.

175
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:38,640
Especially the schoolgirl

176
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:40,220
who wrote the play.

177
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:42,910
This review attacks the government.

178
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,260
That's rather treasonous.

179
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:49,820
A schoolgirl showing her face in public,

180
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:51,500
calling the shots.

181
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:53,630
Just wait and see

182
00:13:53,630 --> 00:13:55,490
which man would dare marry her now.

183
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:57,830
Why make it sound so serious?

184
00:13:57,830 --> 00:13:59,080
Which poor girl is so unlucky

185
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:00,310
as to marry into our family?

186
00:14:01,750 --> 00:14:03,420
Why are you only coming down now?

187
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:04,710
What were you doing last night?

188
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:09,030
She was up late last night,

189
00:14:09,030 --> 00:14:11,280
finishing her homework.

190
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:13,360
What's wrong with letting her sleep in?

191
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:14,620
Exactly, exactly.

192
00:14:14,700 --> 00:14:15,730
I've been working very hard.

193
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:19,220
After we finish eating,

194
00:14:19,220 --> 00:14:20,020
I'll test you myself.

195
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:21,600
Let's see

196
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:23,120
how that new home tutor

197
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:24,440
has been teaching you.

198
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:30,480
Oh, right.

199
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:31,520
Where's Madame Chen?

200
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:32,290
Why haven't I seen her

201
00:14:32,290 --> 00:14:33,220
come down for breakfast?

202
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:35,080
She left first thing this morning,

203
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:36,980
saying she was going to Detianxiang

204
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:38,520
to buy the finest tianma.

205
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:40,320
She plans to stew it for hours

206
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:42,400
to help your father regain his strength.

207
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:44,000
Madame Chen is so thoughtful.

208
00:14:45,620 --> 00:14:47,100
You were just talking

209
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:49,080
about the female playwright

210
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,120
from the Chunfeng Troupe, right?

211
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:52,310
She's incredibly famous now.

212
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:54,240
They say she and the troupe

213
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,900
have been helping those refugees

214
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,280
get their lives in order.

215
00:14:57,280 --> 00:14:57,890
And that's not all.

216
00:14:58,150 --> 00:14:59,560
They're also helping them find work

217
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:00,550
so they can support themselves.

218
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:03,170
That girl is truly remarkable.

219
00:15:05,870 --> 00:15:08,520
Changxuan fined Feng Sanli

220
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:10,220
over a piece of land.

221
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:12,200
Is that the Qingshui Town
from the papers,

222
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:14,590
the one sheltering refugees?

223
00:15:17,590 --> 00:15:19,050
When doing things,

224
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,920
we need to leave room to maneuver,

225
00:15:21,220 --> 00:15:23,660
and be principled, pragmatic,
and restrained.

226
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,220
Look at what Changxuan's done.

227
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:27,220
Who knows how many

228
00:15:27,220 --> 00:15:28,570
uncles and elders he's offended?

229
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:30,040
What about you?

230
00:15:30,820 --> 00:15:32,550
When you first took office,

231
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,450
you took on those old fossils

232
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:35,540
without holding back.

233
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:37,710
My son still has years to learn

234
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:39,680
that ruthless streak from you.

235
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:42,810
What are you laughing at?

236
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:44,760
Eat your food.

237
00:15:56,190 --> 00:15:56,650
Stop

238
00:15:56,650 --> 00:15:57,860
at Li's Preserved Fruits.

239
00:15:58,580 --> 00:15:59,430
Qixuan loves them.

240
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:00,520
I'll buy some.

241
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:37,300
I was actually worried

242
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:38,240
you'd gotten so hooked

243
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:39,060
on being Yu Zhongquan's son-in-law

244
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:41,800
that you forgot what today is.

245
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:52,220
I didn't expect Yu Changxuan

246
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:54,160
to be this capable.

247
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:56,750
Without making a sound,

248
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:58,090
he secured the Ninth Corps.

249
00:16:58,930 --> 00:16:59,890
At this rate,

250
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:03,140
I'm afraid his foothold

251
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:03,920
will only get more solid.

252
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:06,540
Don't worry.

253
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:08,700
I won't let him

254
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:10,090
keep running wild like this.

255
00:17:14,080 --> 00:17:14,600
Bingwen,

256
00:17:16,940 --> 00:17:17,610
if it weren't for you,

257
00:17:17,610 --> 00:17:18,880
Father, and Mother taking me in.

258
00:17:19,840 --> 00:17:20,480
I might have

259
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,620
starved to death on the street.

260
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:23,730
I owe you for that.

261
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:26,250
I chose to repay you willingly.

262
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:28,340
As long as I can avenge

263
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:29,300
Father and Mother with you,

264
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:31,150
I'll do anything you ask.

265
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:34,860
I'm just afraid it'll all be
for nothing.

266
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:36,830
We didn't endure

267
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:37,680
all the hardships

268
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:39,240
to watch the Yu family thrive.

269
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:40,700
Wanqiao,

270
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:43,170
just hold on a little longer.

271
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,310
The revenge we want

272
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:47,830
isn't just taking Yu Zhongquan's life.

273
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,170
Someday,

274
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:54,200
I'll make the entire Yu family

275
00:17:56,870 --> 00:17:58,620
crawl at our feet.

276
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:37,410
What are you two doing here?

277
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:38,900
What do you want?

278
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,110
Just here to chat with you.

279
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:43,750
Don't move.

280
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:44,830
Don't move.

281
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:48,620
Ye Pingjun,

282
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:51,530
you cut my face.

283
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:52,550
Do you think

284
00:18:52,550 --> 00:18:54,040
that I'll let this go

285
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:55,910
just because you cozied up to
Gu Ruitong?

286
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:58,130
You know perfectly well

287
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:00,160
that your injury has nothing to do
with me.

288
00:19:00,600 --> 00:19:01,720
A sharp tongue

289
00:19:02,540 --> 00:19:03,480
won't help you.

290
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:05,360
So, today,

291
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:07,120
I'll teach you a lesson.

292
00:19:22,530 --> 00:19:23,330
Don't try anything.

293
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,010
Nanhuai has laws.

294
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:27,250
The law

295
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:31,010
controls people like you

296
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:33,040
and serves people like me.

297
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:34,340
Got it?

298
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:36,370
Do you really think

299
00:19:36,370 --> 00:19:37,590
you can just get away with it?

300
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:39,380
I'm curious to see

301
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:41,720
what consequences there would be.

302
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:55,590
Stop!

303
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:01,290
Xueting.

304
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:03,160
What are you doing?

305
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:06,990
Ye Pingjun,

306
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:08,980
how many men have you been

307
00:20:09,010 --> 00:20:10,150
stringing along?

308
00:20:10,970 --> 00:20:12,380
One after another, they come to
your rescue.

309
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,100
What's your name?

310
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:15,880
Why are you bullying a classmate?

311
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,760
Do you know she is

312
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:18,900
the daughter of President Tao

313
00:20:18,900 --> 00:20:20,320
of Tonghui Bank?

314
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:26,160
That title implies noble character.

315
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:27,660
Yet you use your power to bully others.

316
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:28,490
Shame on you!

317
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:29,820
You little brat!

318
00:20:29,820 --> 00:20:32,010
Vulgar words and vile behavior.

319
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:33,140
I don't care

320
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:34,020
whose precious daughter you are.

321
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:35,490
All I see is

322
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:38,280
appalling rudeness.

323
00:20:48,660 --> 00:20:49,170
We're here.

324
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:51,730
Let's get out.

325
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:54,860
Come.

326
00:20:57,980 --> 00:20:58,360
Come.

327
00:20:58,960 --> 00:20:59,480
Mu.

328
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:00,680
Careful.

329
00:21:04,660 --> 00:21:06,310
Thank you so much, Mr. Yu,

330
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:08,140
for picking up Mu and An from
the hospital

331
00:21:08,370 --> 00:21:09,800
and driving us home.

332
00:21:10,460 --> 00:21:11,120
These snacks

333
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:11,980
are for the kids.

334
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,000
Thank you, Mr. Yu.

335
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:15,380
Thank you, Changxuan.

336
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,230
You're welcome.

337
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:17,510
Mr. Yu,

338
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:18,480
you're here.

339
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:19,240
Ms. Wang.

340
00:21:19,620 --> 00:21:20,180
Mu, An.

341
00:21:20,520 --> 00:21:21,180
You're back.

342
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:22,000
Mr. Zhao,

343
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:23,200
do we have enough help today?

344
00:21:23,280 --> 00:21:25,040
Kids need to bathe, disinfect in shifts,

345
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:26,020
and change into fresh clothes.

346
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:26,480
More than enough.

347
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:27,640
The Charity Union

348
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:28,750
sent over lots of volunteers.

349
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:29,520
Also,

350
00:21:29,820 --> 00:21:30,940
the Chunfeng Troupe

351
00:21:31,020 --> 00:21:31,490
is here too.

352
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:32,740
Mr. Yu,

353
00:21:32,940 --> 00:21:34,320
I'll take the kids inside first, then.

354
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:35,780
Changxuan,

355
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:37,400
can you play with us?

356
00:21:37,940 --> 00:21:38,600
Mu, be good.

357
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:39,890
Changxuan is very busy.

358
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:41,190
We've already troubled him enough.

359
00:21:41,230 --> 00:21:41,650
It's fine.

360
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:43,540
I'm free today.

361
00:21:47,590 --> 00:21:48,810
Person.

362
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:49,750
Mouth.

363
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:51,260
Mouth.

364
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:52,380
Hand.

365
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:53,620
Hand.

366
00:21:53,920 --> 00:21:54,800
That's right, very good.

367
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:55,580
Any of you

368
00:21:55,580 --> 00:21:56,980
want to try reading them aloud?

369
00:22:02,580 --> 00:22:02,980
Mr. Yu,

370
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:04,150
this way, please.

371
00:22:07,310 --> 00:22:08,180
The union's representatives

372
00:22:08,590 --> 00:22:10,440
watched the Chunfeng Troupe's
performance.

373
00:22:10,690 --> 00:22:11,340
They were deeply moved.

374
00:22:11,780 --> 00:22:12,300
After they returned,

375
00:22:12,460 --> 00:22:13,890
they set up this place

376
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:15,200
for the refugees

377
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:16,570
as a temporary settlement.

378
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:18,410
Everyone has changed a lot.

379
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:20,990
The Chunfeng Troupe sent teachers over

380
00:22:21,170 --> 00:22:22,410
to teach everyone to read and write.

381
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:24,420
And they even found jobs

382
00:22:24,420 --> 00:22:25,130
for these women.

383
00:22:25,500 --> 00:22:27,190
Thanks to Director Liang and Miss Ye,

384
00:22:27,470 --> 00:22:28,500
who applied to the Charity Union

385
00:22:28,500 --> 00:22:29,520
for a vacant plot of land

386
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,020
and distributed seeds and fertilizer.

387
00:22:31,910 --> 00:22:32,830
Miss Ye said

388
00:22:33,140 --> 00:22:34,580
relief assistance isn't
a long-term solution.

389
00:22:34,980 --> 00:22:35,930
We need to help these refugees

390
00:22:35,930 --> 00:22:37,040
learn self-sufficiency.

391
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:38,520
This way.

392
00:22:38,780 --> 00:22:39,260
The backyard

393
00:22:39,420 --> 00:22:40,460
is where the children live.

394
00:22:41,020 --> 00:22:41,540
Let's go.

395
00:22:44,540 --> 00:22:45,400
Sit down and behave.

396
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:19,680
Pingjun.

397
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:41,110
Mr. Yu,

398
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:43,100
what brings you here today?

399
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:48,340
Do I have to report to you?

400
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:51,870
Why are you suddenly upset?

401
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:57,120
You think some empty gestures

402
00:23:57,350 --> 00:23:58,720
and teaching them to read a few words

403
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:00,510
will solve their livelihood problems?

404
00:24:02,820 --> 00:24:03,470
What else, then?

405
00:24:04,580 --> 00:24:05,430
Mr. Yu,

406
00:24:05,780 --> 00:24:07,420
would you rather they go begging?

407
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:09,500
So, in your eyes,

408
00:24:09,900 --> 00:24:11,230
they only deserve handouts,

409
00:24:11,570 --> 00:24:12,810
living like ants?

410
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:14,290
They never accept

411
00:24:14,290 --> 00:24:15,140
charity offered with contempt.

412
00:24:15,790 --> 00:24:16,420
They can also

413
00:24:16,420 --> 00:24:17,660
be self-reliant

414
00:24:17,660 --> 00:24:18,340
with their meager strength.

415
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:21,820
Self-reliant?

416
00:24:23,980 --> 00:24:25,240
Every brick and tile here

417
00:24:26,080 --> 00:24:27,490
came from Nanhuai.

418
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:33,260
I can let them stay

419
00:24:34,800 --> 00:24:36,440
or send them away anytime.

420
00:24:40,940 --> 00:24:41,410
Right.

421
00:24:42,360 --> 00:24:44,240
Mr. Yu, one stomp of your foot

422
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:46,180
can drive them all out.

423
00:24:46,940 --> 00:24:47,730
If you look down

424
00:24:47,730 --> 00:24:48,540
on what we do,

425
00:24:48,820 --> 00:24:50,230
don't grace us with your presence,

426
00:24:51,060 --> 00:24:52,250
lest we dirty your precious feet.

427
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,440
Ye Pingjun, you've gotten bold.

428
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:01,140
How dare you talk to me like that?

429
00:25:02,700 --> 00:25:03,560
Am I wrong?

430
00:25:04,760 --> 00:25:05,690
They don't want to become

431
00:25:05,690 --> 00:25:06,620
a burden to Nanhuai.

432
00:25:07,060 --> 00:25:08,320
They're refugees now,

433
00:25:09,060 --> 00:25:10,610
but that doesn't mean they'll
stay that way.

434
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:13,340
Even wildflowers and weeds

435
00:25:13,340 --> 00:25:14,340
have lives of their own.

436
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:17,010
Even on the most barren soil,

437
00:25:17,600 --> 00:25:19,360
if given even a sliver of hope,

438
00:25:20,120 --> 00:25:21,520
they'll struggle to put down roots

439
00:25:21,900 --> 00:25:22,850
and grow toward the sky.

440
00:25:42,160 --> 00:25:43,260
Why aren't you saying anything?

441
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:56,660
These people stay unregistered

442
00:25:57,900 --> 00:25:59,540
no matter how they struggle.

443
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:01,130
Putting down roots?

444
00:26:01,620 --> 00:26:02,480
Easier said than done.

445
00:26:02,940 --> 00:26:05,280
I hope you don't work yourselves ragged

446
00:26:06,180 --> 00:26:07,140
only to end up with nothing.

447
00:26:10,580 --> 00:26:11,380
Mr. Yu, you don't need

448
00:26:11,380 --> 00:26:12,540
to worry about that.

449
00:26:13,380 --> 00:26:14,280
You must be very busy.

450
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:15,880
Please head back.

451
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:41,780
Come in.

452
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:44,530
Mr. Yu.

453
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:46,540
Look.

454
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:47,850
In this round of hiring,

455
00:26:47,970 --> 00:26:49,550
this candidate topped the written test,

456
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:50,260
a full 50 points

457
00:26:50,260 --> 00:26:51,260
above second place.

458
00:26:53,340 --> 00:26:54,030
But I strongly advise

459
00:26:54,030 --> 00:26:56,140
against hiring him.

460
00:26:56,960 --> 00:26:57,460
Why?

461
00:26:58,290 --> 00:27:00,420
This guy is way too arrogant.

462
00:27:00,980 --> 00:27:01,540
He said

463
00:27:01,540 --> 00:27:02,990
the Mauser C96s we purchased

464
00:27:03,030 --> 00:27:04,100
are outdated equipment.

465
00:27:04,660 --> 00:27:04,960
Yes.

466
00:27:04,960 --> 00:27:06,200
He does have a point.

467
00:27:06,780 --> 00:27:07,270
But he started

468
00:27:07,270 --> 00:27:08,260
telling his superiors what to do.

469
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:10,120
No respect for rank whatsoever.

470
00:27:10,260 --> 00:27:10,990
Who does he think he is?

471
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:13,860
This letter is from Jiang Xueting,

472
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:15,290
her fiancé.

473
00:27:22,520 --> 00:27:23,840
Of those we hired this time,

474
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:24,750
how many are

475
00:27:25,240 --> 00:27:25,880
German translators?

476
00:27:27,860 --> 00:27:29,660
People who know German and military gear

477
00:27:29,660 --> 00:27:30,540
are really scarce.

478
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:32,190
We barely managed to pick three.

479
00:27:33,420 --> 00:27:34,710
The weapon materials to translate

480
00:27:34,710 --> 00:27:35,520
are massive.

481
00:27:36,380 --> 00:27:37,160
Three people aren't enough.

482
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:40,420
So, you're saying...?

483
00:27:40,900 --> 00:27:42,320
Add Jiang Xueting.

484
00:27:44,160 --> 00:27:44,540
Yes.

485
00:27:58,340 --> 00:27:58,980
You report tomorrow.

486
00:28:00,960 --> 00:28:01,440
Okay.

487
00:28:01,760 --> 00:28:02,850
I'll report on time tomorrow.

488
00:28:10,520 --> 00:28:11,020
Pingjun.

489
00:28:12,280 --> 00:28:12,790
Xueting.

490
00:28:15,100 --> 00:28:16,440
What's got you so happy?

491
00:28:17,190 --> 00:28:18,630
I'm reporting to the Ninth General Staff

492
00:28:18,630 --> 00:28:19,600
of the Yu Army tomorrow.

493
00:28:19,900 --> 00:28:20,800
My position is Secretary-Translator.

494
00:28:26,380 --> 00:28:26,980
What's wrong?

495
00:28:27,420 --> 00:28:28,440
You look so pale.

496
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:32,760
Weren't you going to work at
a newspaper?

497
00:28:33,080 --> 00:28:35,220
Why the sudden switch to the military?

498
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:37,940
I want to get some
military experience first

499
00:28:38,180 --> 00:28:38,880
to broaden my horizons.

500
00:28:39,080 --> 00:28:39,940
I'll go to the newspaper later.

501
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:46,600
Is something bothering you?

502
00:28:52,160 --> 00:28:54,100
A while ago,

503
00:28:54,280 --> 00:28:55,340
while working as a copyist

504
00:28:55,340 --> 00:28:56,840
at the Yuchun Theatre
of the Hsiang Hsi Hotel,

505
00:28:57,520 --> 00:28:59,130
I got caught up in
an assassination case.

506
00:28:59,840 --> 00:29:00,800
Yu Changxuan

507
00:29:00,940 --> 00:29:02,370
mistakenly thought I was a suspect.

508
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:04,410
Between us,

509
00:29:04,740 --> 00:29:06,090
there's some bad blood.

510
00:29:06,680 --> 00:29:07,680
Did they give you a hard time?

511
00:29:08,160 --> 00:29:09,040
No, not at all.

512
00:29:09,600 --> 00:29:10,930
After everything was cleared up,

513
00:29:10,930 --> 00:29:12,060
they let me go.

514
00:29:12,580 --> 00:29:13,580
My concern is

515
00:29:13,580 --> 00:29:15,160
that this might affect you.

516
00:29:17,660 --> 00:29:18,330
Don't worry.

517
00:29:18,880 --> 00:29:19,890
This is just temporary.

518
00:29:20,460 --> 00:29:21,470
I'm in a civilian role.

519
00:29:21,900 --> 00:29:22,480
I won't have much contact

520
00:29:22,480 --> 00:29:23,170
with them.

521
00:29:24,860 --> 00:29:25,700
After some time has passed,

522
00:29:26,340 --> 00:29:27,260
I'll find another job,

523
00:29:27,760 --> 00:29:28,590
one that's more stable.

524
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:36,280
Okay.

525
00:29:37,320 --> 00:29:38,520
But you have to be careful.

526
00:29:54,540 --> 00:29:55,220
The Corps Commander is here.

527
00:30:12,180 --> 00:30:12,580
Sit.

528
00:30:14,980 --> 00:30:16,390
Welcome, translation specialists,

529
00:30:16,600 --> 00:30:17,880
to the Ninth Corps.

530
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:19,960
You all excelled in both the written

531
00:30:19,960 --> 00:30:20,800
and oral exams,

532
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:23,310
emerging as the best of the best.

533
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:26,810
Anyone who won't pursue great dreams

534
00:30:27,330 --> 00:30:29,300
wastes the life they've been given.

535
00:30:30,060 --> 00:30:31,100
My guiding principle

536
00:30:31,780 --> 00:30:32,540
is innovation.

537
00:30:32,970 --> 00:30:34,220
I want the Yu Army

538
00:30:34,840 --> 00:30:36,100
to have the most advanced arms

539
00:30:36,100 --> 00:30:36,890
and equipment of the day.

540
00:30:37,300 --> 00:30:38,930
Outdated weapons must never

541
00:30:40,020 --> 00:30:41,380
cost the lives of our soldiers

542
00:30:42,100 --> 00:30:42,780
for nothing.

543
00:30:44,140 --> 00:30:44,770
The General Staff

544
00:30:45,260 --> 00:30:46,220
will send you the latest materials

545
00:30:46,220 --> 00:30:47,530
about the German weapons daily.

546
00:30:48,180 --> 00:30:49,680
Please translate everything

547
00:30:49,950 --> 00:30:51,160
from weapon performance specifications

548
00:30:51,160 --> 00:30:51,830
to the manufacturing processes.

549
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:53,700
Of the four of you,

550
00:30:54,220 --> 00:30:55,240
only Bao Shijie

551
00:30:55,740 --> 00:30:57,070
has a background as an officer cadet
in Japan

552
00:30:57,820 --> 00:30:59,210
and knows firearms well.

553
00:31:00,040 --> 00:31:00,680
So, for now,

554
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:01,740
he'll serve as acting team leader.

555
00:31:02,940 --> 00:31:03,360
Yes, sir.

556
00:31:04,580 --> 00:31:05,520
I look forward to working with you all

557
00:31:05,760 --> 00:31:06,710
from now on.

558
00:31:08,520 --> 00:31:09,180
All right, everyone.

559
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:10,460
You'll be taken

560
00:31:10,460 --> 00:31:11,350
to report to the Translation Office.

561
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:13,120
You can start work today.

562
00:31:19,820 --> 00:31:20,520
Jiang Xueting.

563
00:31:25,550 --> 00:31:25,920
Come here.

564
00:31:30,980 --> 00:31:31,880
Mr. Yu, what's wrong?

565
00:31:33,720 --> 00:31:35,190
You graduated from
the Department of International Politics

566
00:31:35,290 --> 00:31:37,030
of Waseda University.

567
00:31:37,470 --> 00:31:38,710
You excelled in every subject,

568
00:31:39,680 --> 00:31:41,000
and you're a gifted writer.

569
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:44,100
You should have plenty of options.

570
00:31:45,480 --> 00:31:46,620
So, why join the military?

571
00:31:47,750 --> 00:31:49,280
You're recruiting foreign translators

572
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:50,600
and reforming the military.

573
00:31:50,860 --> 00:31:51,620
I imagine

574
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:54,710
you must be a forward-thinking,

575
00:31:55,240 --> 00:31:56,470
broad-minded commander.

576
00:31:57,220 --> 00:31:58,280
Under your command,

577
00:31:58,280 --> 00:31:59,170
I'm sure I can accomplish great things.

578
00:31:59,540 --> 00:32:01,640
Then, my years of study won't be wasted.

579
00:32:03,820 --> 00:32:04,280
Good.

580
00:32:05,360 --> 00:32:06,620
I don't care about rank or background.

581
00:32:07,400 --> 00:32:08,300
Only ability matters.

582
00:32:09,500 --> 00:32:10,640
Thank you for the honor.

583
00:32:13,100 --> 00:32:14,050
How many people are in your family?

584
00:32:20,220 --> 00:32:21,150
My parents passed away early.

585
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:23,140
As for family,

586
00:32:24,800 --> 00:32:25,980
I do have a fiancée.

587
00:32:26,920 --> 00:32:27,760
Her mother

588
00:32:28,320 --> 00:32:29,560
and my mother are sworn sisters.

589
00:32:35,100 --> 00:32:36,680
Then, you should work even harder.

590
00:32:38,140 --> 00:32:39,420
Someday, your fiancée

591
00:32:39,900 --> 00:32:40,780
and your mother-in-law

592
00:32:41,600 --> 00:32:43,640
will both rely on you.

593
00:32:48,160 --> 00:32:49,050
I'll keep that in mind.

594
00:33:04,720 --> 00:33:06,510
The chicken is finally stewed tender.

595
00:33:12,340 --> 00:33:13,820
Take this chicken soup to Xueting

596
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:15,180
while it's hot.

597
00:33:18,040 --> 00:33:19,330
Isn't it too late?

598
00:33:19,330 --> 00:33:20,840
He might have already eaten.

599
00:33:21,140 --> 00:33:21,930
Cafeteria food

600
00:33:21,930 --> 00:33:23,810
can't beat a home-cooked meal.

601
00:33:24,620 --> 00:33:25,440
Come on.

602
00:33:26,940 --> 00:33:28,100
Just take it over.

603
00:33:30,420 --> 00:33:31,180
Hurry up.

604
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:33,140
Go on, go on.

605
00:33:34,620 --> 00:33:35,060
Once you've delivered it,

606
00:33:35,060 --> 00:33:36,290
come right back for chicken soup.

607
00:33:36,980 --> 00:33:37,620
Got it.

608
00:33:47,660 --> 00:33:47,940
Hello?

609
00:33:48,700 --> 00:33:49,260
Secretary Jiang,

610
00:33:49,460 --> 00:33:50,620
Miss Ye is here to see you.

611
00:33:51,920 --> 00:33:52,420
Got it.

612
00:34:15,060 --> 00:34:15,590
Xueting.

613
00:34:17,040 --> 00:34:18,600
Why did you come out without
an umbrella?

614
00:34:19,040 --> 00:34:19,800
What are you doing here?

615
00:34:20,080 --> 00:34:21,960
Mother made you chicken soup
and sent me over.

616
00:34:40,200 --> 00:34:40,870
How long have you been waiting?

617
00:34:41,220 --> 00:34:41,950
Your hair's all wet.

618
00:34:52,620 --> 00:34:53,420
In this heavy rain,

619
00:34:53,920 --> 00:34:54,700
you shouldn't have come.

620
00:34:54,700 --> 00:34:55,600
What if you catch a cold?

621
00:34:57,120 --> 00:34:57,770
I'm fine.

622
00:34:58,080 --> 00:34:59,360
When I headed out today,

623
00:34:59,360 --> 00:35:00,340
it wasn't raining this hard.

624
00:35:00,660 --> 00:35:02,000
But once I was out, it got worse.

625
00:35:02,200 --> 00:35:02,850
Bad call.

626
00:35:15,700 --> 00:35:16,080
Okay, okay.

627
00:35:16,380 --> 00:35:16,980
Go on back.

628
00:35:17,200 --> 00:35:18,060
I'll get you a rickshaw.

629
00:35:18,360 --> 00:35:19,180
No, no need.

630
00:35:19,440 --> 00:35:20,780
Hard to get one in this rain.

631
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:22,170
Hurry, take this inside.

632
00:35:22,240 --> 00:35:23,640
It won't taste good once it gets cold.

633
00:35:24,060 --> 00:35:24,440
Go on.

634
00:35:24,580 --> 00:35:25,120
Don't overwork yourself.

635
00:35:25,120 --> 00:35:25,780
Ye Pingjun?

636
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:30,600
What's going on with you two?

637
00:35:31,940 --> 00:35:32,360
Then,

638
00:35:32,900 --> 00:35:33,820
I'll head back now.

639
00:35:40,360 --> 00:35:41,780
You don't even greet your superior?

640
00:35:42,480 --> 00:35:43,460
How rude.

641
00:35:53,340 --> 00:35:54,030
Oh, I see.

642
00:35:55,400 --> 00:35:56,740
Could those two be...

643
00:36:01,100 --> 00:36:01,500
Mr. Yu,

644
00:36:01,920 --> 00:36:03,400
your 15 classmates from
the military academy

645
00:36:03,540 --> 00:36:04,480
have all taken up their posts.

646
00:36:05,060 --> 00:36:06,060
Wu Zuoxiao is now acting

647
00:36:06,060 --> 00:36:06,950
in Huang Dakui's position

648
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:08,480
as commander of the 27th Regiment.

649
00:36:09,740 --> 00:36:10,910
Tell them to act without holding back.

650
00:36:11,120 --> 00:36:11,990
They shouldn't worry so much.

651
00:36:12,360 --> 00:36:13,720
Big news, guys!

652
00:36:14,020 --> 00:36:15,520
I've got a major scoop.

653
00:36:15,520 --> 00:36:16,120
Let me tell you.

654
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:17,880
You'll definitely want to hear it.

655
00:36:22,120 --> 00:36:22,700
Go on.

656
00:36:24,020 --> 00:36:24,560
I...

657
00:36:24,600 --> 00:36:26,040
This is no fun.

658
00:36:26,300 --> 00:36:26,740
I'm telling you.

659
00:36:26,840 --> 00:36:27,960
Don't you want to know

660
00:36:28,280 --> 00:36:30,160
who Jiang Xueting's girlfriend is?

661
00:36:34,340 --> 00:36:34,980
You two

662
00:36:35,050 --> 00:36:36,060
could rack your brains

663
00:36:36,060 --> 00:36:37,620
and still never guess.

664
00:36:38,950 --> 00:36:40,160
Jiang Xueting's girlfriend

665
00:36:40,460 --> 00:36:41,140
is actually

666
00:36:42,680 --> 00:36:43,700
Ye Pingjun.

667
00:36:45,200 --> 00:36:45,700
I know.

668
00:36:45,700 --> 00:36:47,220
I know it's hard to believe.

669
00:36:47,900 --> 00:36:49,800
I couldn't believe it either.

670
00:36:49,800 --> 00:36:50,440
But on my way back,

671
00:36:50,440 --> 00:36:51,330
I saw it with my own eyes.

672
00:36:51,660 --> 00:36:52,240
Man,

673
00:36:52,390 --> 00:36:53,820
it was pouring rain.

674
00:36:53,890 --> 00:36:54,580
And Ye Pingjun

675
00:36:54,580 --> 00:36:55,650
personally brought soup to
Jiang Xueting.

676
00:36:56,080 --> 00:36:57,190
What are the odds?

677
00:36:57,500 --> 00:36:57,920
Right?

678
00:36:59,620 --> 00:37:00,160
Well.

679
00:37:00,260 --> 00:37:01,080
Show them around

680
00:37:01,080 --> 00:37:02,300
the workspace and workflow.

681
00:37:02,300 --> 00:37:03,020
After all, they just got here.

682
00:37:03,880 --> 00:37:04,320
Don't worry.

683
00:37:04,440 --> 00:37:05,010
I'll handle it.

684
00:37:05,800 --> 00:37:06,780
What are you talking about?

685
00:37:07,640 --> 00:37:08,760
You're not surprised at all?

686
00:37:16,920 --> 00:37:17,680
Now, I get it.

687
00:37:18,770 --> 00:37:19,700
No wonder you insisted

688
00:37:19,700 --> 00:37:21,180
on adding Jiang Xueting.

689
00:37:21,660 --> 00:37:22,760
So, you knew all along

690
00:37:22,760 --> 00:37:23,660
he's Ye Pingjun's boyfriend.

691
00:37:23,700 --> 00:37:24,900
You kept him close on purpose,

692
00:37:24,900 --> 00:37:25,240
didn't you?

693
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:32,600
In my office,

694
00:37:32,600 --> 00:37:33,960
no talking about that nonsense.

695
00:37:34,400 --> 00:37:36,020
This office is for
military matters only.

696
00:37:39,080 --> 00:37:41,270
If you won't answer me directly,

697
00:37:41,680 --> 00:37:42,930
I'll take that as a yes.

698
00:37:46,040 --> 00:37:47,480
If you have too much free time,

699
00:37:47,820 --> 00:37:48,720
I'll transfer you

700
00:37:48,720 --> 00:37:50,460
to the quarry in the suburbs
as a supervisor.

701
00:37:50,880 --> 00:37:52,000
No, no, don't.

702
00:37:52,340 --> 00:37:54,350
I'm just fooling around.
Why take it seriously?

703
00:37:54,660 --> 00:37:55,690
This is no fun anymore.

704
00:37:56,260 --> 00:37:56,760
You two talk.

705
00:38:03,300 --> 00:38:04,120
Show them the ropes.

706
00:38:04,780 --> 00:38:05,080
Yes, sir.

707
00:38:14,460 --> 00:38:15,670
That explains it.

708
00:38:16,020 --> 00:38:17,260
When she was sick,

709
00:38:17,260 --> 00:38:18,350
he even went to see her in secret.

710
00:38:19,920 --> 00:38:20,740
And then,

711
00:38:20,740 --> 00:38:22,410
he had you get her away

712
00:38:22,700 --> 00:38:23,870
from Tao Xili

713
00:38:23,910 --> 00:38:24,950
under Lanqing's name.

714
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:26,300
And now,

715
00:38:26,620 --> 00:38:28,520
he's put her real boyfriend

716
00:38:28,520 --> 00:38:29,390
in the army.

717
00:38:31,660 --> 00:38:32,870
When has he ever

718
00:38:32,870 --> 00:38:33,650
gone to such lengths

719
00:38:34,340 --> 00:38:35,480
for a girl?

720
00:38:42,420 --> 00:38:43,400
Ruitong.

721
00:38:44,840 --> 00:38:45,240
I...

722
00:38:45,610 --> 00:38:47,020
Is your brain made of wood?

723
00:38:48,420 --> 00:38:50,020
We're talking about love here.

724
00:38:50,020 --> 00:38:51,470
Do you understand? Love.

725
00:38:51,940 --> 00:38:53,280
It's the kind of love that makes

726
00:38:53,280 --> 00:38:56,160
the sun, moon, and stars all dim.

727
00:38:59,120 --> 00:38:59,810
Could you please

728
00:38:59,810 --> 00:39:01,240
play along with me a little

729
00:39:01,240 --> 00:39:02,820
and give me some kind of reaction?

730
00:39:06,980 --> 00:39:08,360
That has nothing to do with my duties.

731
00:39:13,340 --> 00:39:14,600
Oh, my silly brother.

732
00:39:15,060 --> 00:39:17,240
Duties aren't everything in life.

733
00:39:18,100 --> 00:39:19,520
Once you've tasted love,

734
00:39:19,880 --> 00:39:20,650
you'll understand.

735
00:39:20,990 --> 00:39:22,570
Even the toughest man

736
00:39:23,400 --> 00:39:24,980
can be completely transformed.

737
00:39:28,940 --> 00:39:29,620
Where are you going?

738
00:39:30,220 --> 00:39:31,440
All this pretending.

739
00:39:31,940 --> 00:39:32,570
I'm telling you.

740
00:39:32,760 --> 00:39:34,180
Mr. Yu is truly in love.

741
00:39:34,180 --> 00:39:34,800
Just believe me.

742
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:35,470
Can you help me?

743
00:40:36,720 --> 00:40:37,900
My hair's tangled.

744
00:42:58,360 --> 00:42:59,160
Seven.

745
00:43:00,780 --> 00:43:01,560
Eight.

746
00:43:02,140 --> 00:43:02,780
Nine.

747
00:43:08,020 --> 00:43:08,480
Ten.

748
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:15,700
Mr. Yu,

749
00:43:17,100 --> 00:43:18,040
I have a proposal.

750
00:43:18,960 --> 00:43:19,900
A proposal?

751
00:43:19,900 --> 00:43:20,300
That's right.

752
00:43:21,420 --> 00:43:22,500
Do you dare make this bet with me?

753
00:43:27,060 --> 00:43:27,920
You monster!

754
00:43:42,000 --> 00:43:43,040
I'll ask you again.

755
00:43:44,740 --> 00:43:45,620
Who am I to you?
